[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"497","stub":{"id":"497","section":"Windy Hill Rd to Chattahoochee River","altname":"","river":"Rottenwood Creek","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-GEO"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"8","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"Put-In on 1 North Parkway.","id":"444","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Put-In","distance":"0","photoID":null,"difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"hazard","description":"A double ledge drop. The left bank is undercut. At high flows this rapid creats a nasty riverwide hole, backed up by a second large hole.  At higher flows it can be snuck down the right.   At low flows you run down the meat on the left.","id":"443","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Confederate Life","distance":"0.2","photoID":"1679","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"Nice little double ledge with a shallow playhole.","id":"458","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Windy Ridge Parkway Bridge Rapid","distance":"0.6","difficulty":"III","approximate":false,"photoID":"1681"},{"type":"hazard","description":"Just above the Akers Mill parking area is a riverwide pipe.  At low flows it can be ducked under, at higher flows its a hazard with not much of an eddy above it.","id":"6350","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"First Pipe","distance":"0.9","photoID":"0","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"playspot","description":"After crossing under the I-285 interstate bridges the river turns to the right the back to the left. Scout Akers Mill Rapid on the left. The current is split by a large boulder. Beware or rebar in the approach to the rapid. The standard line is down the right. Continuous Class 3 water follow for the next quarter mile. There are two good play waves in this stretch.","id":"445","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Akers Mill Rapid","distance":"1","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":"1677"},{"type":"portage","description":"Big riverwide sewer pipe. Lots of wood on the upstream side. Carry on the left.","id":"446","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Sewage Pipe","distance":"1.75","photoID":"6381","difficulty":null,"approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"The take-out is on river right at Palisades Park off of Highway 41.","id":"447","location":{"latitude":"0","longitude":"0"},"name":"Metro Hooch Takeout","distance":"2.25","photoID":null,"difficulty":"I","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[{"id":"6378","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5672","description":"Akers Mill is the most technical rapid on Rottenwood. The lines change with water level. Here Milt Aitken takes the river left line as Jim Kelly takes the meatier river right \"pollution-in-your-face\" line.","caption":"(RM) Akers Mill","poi_name":"Akers Mill","subject":"Milt Aitken & Jim Kelly","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"447","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6378","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6378"}},{"id":"17065","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9505","description":"The Google Earth map is old and shows incomplete construction but the path is accurate for water flow. For more info about Rottenwood Creek, check out http://www.ccgallery.net/rottenwood/","caption":"Upper Rottenwood Creek - Georgia","poi_name":"","subject":"This is Rottenwood Creek from Put-In to Aker's Mill","author":"Chuck - via Google Earth","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/17065","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/17065"}},{"id":"885534","ext":"png","post_id":"888347","description":"a better view of the ledge hole undercut","caption":"undercut Ledge Hole close up","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Rick Thompson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885534","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885534"}},{"id":"39622","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9841","description":"Above Bunker rapid, this rapid is not mentioned in this creeks info page but I thought it was worth taking some pictures of .","caption":"39622.jpeg","poi_name":"Bunker","subject":"","author":"Tommy Mode","poi_id":"458","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/39622","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/39622"}},{"id":"1679","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1344","description":"Run the top tongue left to right.  The entire river left shelf is undercut.  There is about 20 feet between the first and second ledge.","caption":"Confederate Life","poi_name":"Confederate Life","subject":"Jim Strickland","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":"443","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1679","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1679"}},{"id":"6377","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5672","description":"Milt Aitken running Windy Ridge Parkway rapid at a medium high level.","caption":"(RM) Windy Ridge Parkway","poi_name":"Windy Ridge Parkway","subject":"Milt Aitken","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"458","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6377","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6377"}},{"id":"1681","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1344","description":"Second major rapid","caption":"Rottenwood Creek","poi_name":"","subject":"Jim Strickland","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1681","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1681"}},{"id":"6381","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5672","description":"Jim Kelly portaging around \"The Pipe\". The pipe is located near the end of the run.","caption":"(RM) Portaging the Pipe","poi_name":"The Pipe","subject":"Jim Kelly","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6381","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6381"}},{"id":"6379","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5672","description":"Milt Aitken and Jim Kelly eddy out below Akers Mill.","caption":"(RM) Akers Mill wash out","poi_name":"Akers Mill","subject":"Milt Aitken & Jim Kelly","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"447","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6379","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6379"}},{"id":"6380","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5672","description":"Milt Aitken examines Rottenwood's natural beauty at the Pipe. You know things are bad when the prettiest thing on the river is Milt!","caption":"(RM) The Pipe and Natural Beauty","poi_name":"The Pipe","subject":"Milt Aitken","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6380","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6380"}},{"id":"885533","ext":"png","post_id":"888346","description":"dont go there","caption":"Undercut Ledge Hole","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"Rick Thompson","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/885533","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/885533"}},{"id":"1677","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1343","description":"","caption":"Top of Akers Mill Rapid","poi_name":"Akers Mill Rapid","subject":"Jim Strickland","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":"447","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1677","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1677"}},{"id":"1683","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1344","description":"","caption":"Bottom of Akers Mill","poi_name":"Akers Mill Rapid","subject":"Jim Strickland","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":"445","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1683","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1683"}},{"id":"1680","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1343","description":"The run out of the first big drop.  Big old school boats rule!!","caption":"Confederate Life - 2","poi_name":"Confederate Life","subject":"Bradley","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":"443","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1680","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1680"}},{"id":"1682","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1344","description":"Middle of the rapid, after the entrance ledge and S-turn move.","caption":"Akers Mill - 2","poi_name":"Akers Mill Rapid","subject":"Jim Strickland","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":"445","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/1682","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/1682"}},{"id":"6376","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"5672","description":"Jim Kelly running Confederate Life at a medium high level.","caption":"(RM) Confederate Life","poi_name":"Confederate Life","subject":"Jim Kelly","author":"Rob Maxwell","poi_id":"443","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6376","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6376"}},{"id":"39621","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"9841","description":"Picture of Tommy Mode on top of trench (bunker) cut into gorge wall this is directly above what I refer to as bunker rapid . ","caption":"Rottenwood","poi_name":"Bunker Rapid","subject":"Tommy Mode","author":"Tommy Mode","poi_id":"458","photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/39621","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/39621"}}],"detail":{"id":"497","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"**Gauge Description:**\n\nVisual from one of many bridge overpasses. (Delk, Terrill Mill, Windy Hill, Windy Ridge, Interstate North, I-285, and Akers Mill)\n\nRottenwood only runs after heavy rains, and runs off quickly.  It can spike up and down over 1000 cfs in less than an hour.\n\n**November 2007**: USGS now has an online gauge. It does not corelate with the Maxwell gauge. REPORT YOUR RUNS.\n\n_Update 9-01-2003_\\- New Gauge:The gauge is on the Interstate North Parkway SE bridge. It is a painted gauge on the downstream side of the center set of pylons. It is best viewed from river right next to the large 'Interstate North Parkway 180' sign.\n\n0 inchs - passable.  This is around 200 cfs on the USGS gauge.\n\n2 feet - padded.\n\n3 feet - beefy\n\n**River Description:**\n\nRottenwood has some fun whitewater rapids ; The Creek flashes quickly after the rain event and the water is often the color and consistency of a chocolate milk shake. The water quality is not always the best so use good judgement on protective gear.\n\nThe creek is easy to scout from the small hiking park. There is a very nice hiking trail along most of the creek now.\n\nAkers Mill rapid can get into the class 4 range with higher flows.\n\nAbove Akers Mill is a nice ledge drop that resembles a low head dam at higher flows. Beware of the undercut left bank. This drop used to be called Confederate Life, named after the multi-story office building beside it. The building has since changed ownership, currently Ascent Insurance.  See the Rapids tab for more detailed info.\n\nA word of caution would be to watch out for the large (3 to 4 foot diameter) pipe toward the end of the run. At low flows water runs under the pipe, at flood water runs over the pipe. Last checked there was a lot of wood jammed on the upstream side of the pipe, and not much of an eddy above it. Most people carry around the pipe on river left.\n\nRottenwood has been run at some rediculously high levels. Use your best judgement before putting on. If Rottenwood is rising you might find yourself running the rapids dodging mobile strainers, and other assorted trash.\n\nRottenwood and Sope can usually be run back to back with some creative shuttle work.\n\n_Bradley. Posted April 2001, Updated March 2002, revised August 2008._\n\n**Logistics:** The Put-in is just below the Health Club off Windy Hill Rd, on 1 North Parkway. There is a creekside parking area where Poplar Creek drops into Rottenwood Creek.\n\nUse the park on the Hooch at Hwy 41 for a take out. Be current on your Hepatitis shots.\n\nIf your gear is _REALLY_ smelling like an oil spill, there is a car wash about a mile away on Spring Road in Smyrna.\n\n**National Park Service** map of the takeout: [West Palisades](http://www.nps.gov/chat/ppmaps/westpalisades%2Epdf).","averageGradient":"50","maxGradient":"100","length":"2.9","correlations":[{"reachID":"497","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"250","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"ROTTENWOOD CR AT INTERSTATE N PKWY, NR SMYRNA, GA","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"02335910","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"8","dateTime":"2026-05-12T03:00:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"2.28","dateTime":